  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the priority is to establish a simple, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal configuration in the search space: a single modality, single profile, and a standard linear (PCA) encoder. This gives a performance floor for RNA-only modeling and a reference point against which I can later assess whether learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or multimodal fusion actually add value. Starting from the simplest configuration avoids conflating multiple design choices and ensures that any subsequent improvement can be attributed to a specific added component. With 9 experiments remaining, I can then systematically test image-only baselines, encoder comparisons, and multimodal fusion."
}

